# CCO Migration Reconciliation Rules
CCO has imported customers from Cliento and files/journals/images from Google Drive.
Any migration, matching or merge work must follow these rules:
## Sources
- Cliento is the primary source for customer master data.
- Google Drive is the primary source for historical files, images, PDFs and document metadata.
- Do not use Meridiq as a matching source in the Cliento/Drive reconciliation audit unless explicitly requested.
- Never send journal content to external AI.
## Matching
- Detect duplicate patients by personnummer, phone, email, name similarity, birthdate, Drive folder/file names and metadata.
- Always produce a confidence score.
- Always explain why records are considered a match.
- Never auto-merge patients.
- All merge candidates require manual review.
## Data completeness
For every patient, calculate:
- hasClientoRecord
- hasDriveFolder
- driveFileCount
- journalPdfCount
- imageCount
- formCount
- consentCount
- agreementCount
- unknownFileCount
- lowConfidenceFileCount
- missingDriveFileIdCount
- orphanFileCount
- duplicateCandidateCount
- completenessScore
## Merge safety
- Merges must be transactional.
- No data may be deleted during merge.
- Secondary patient must be archived/redirected, not hard deleted.
- All related files, journal PDFs, images, consents, agreements, forms, encounters, notes, metadata and links must move to the primary patient.
- If any transfer fails, rollback the merge.
- Create an audit event and merge manifest for every merge attempt.
- Run post-merge verification.
## UI
Build a Migration QA dashboard with:
- overview counters
- duplicate candidates
- missing data
- unlinked Drive files
- uncertain ?/! files
- merge review
- post-merge verification
Do not mark the task done until we can prove:
- no orphan files remain for approved merges
- file counts match before/after
- no journal PDFs are lost
- no images are lost
- no Drive file IDs are lost
- duplicate patient redirects work
- audit events are created
